    "narrative": "With the season entering its final stages, the Austin Waves face a limited slate today, leaving us to rely on our active options in **Liam Hicks** and **Brayan Rocchio**. **Liam Hicks** earns the nod as our strongest play with a 52.87 score; he benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Armstrong, whose 4.35 xERA provides a clear lane for production. The dynamic platoon advantage (R) paired with his current hot streak moves him safely into the marginal-to-strong threshold. Conversely, **Brayan Rocchio** sits at a 47.20, hampered primarily by his placement in the #9 hole. While the matchup against Martinez (4.63 xERA) is technically favorable, the lack of lineup protection and the inherent difficulty of driving in runs from the bottom of the order drag his efficiency score down toward our start-bench threshold.\n\nOur bench remains stagnant today due to a league-wide scheduling lull. The decision to keep our core\u2014including **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**\u2014on the bench is purely tactical, as they have no games scheduled. The most frustrating development remains **Luis Robert Jr.**, whose continued IL status keeps him unavailable despite the potential roster gap. Looking ahead, we are monitoring the health and potential promotion status of **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jordan Westburg** to bolster the top of the order, as our current lack of depth behind **Liam Hicks** is forcing us to stretch thin on days where our marquee names are idle. We are avoiding any risks today regarding weather or late-inning fatigue, as we are simply waiting for the roster to return to full strength.",
